### Backend

- Keep business rules out of transport handlers and controllers.
- Model data explicitly and ship reversible migrations for schema changes.
- Define request and response contracts and validate every input at the boundary.
- Enforce authentication and authorization on the server for every protected operation.
- Never log secrets or personal data, and return generic error messages to clients.
- Add indexes for query patterns you introduce and avoid unbounded result sets.
- Make background jobs idempotent and safe to retry.
